  "summary": "Proteome-scale purification, yield, structure-search and recoding studies now pair predictive models with explicit calibration or provenance checks.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is that computational predictions in protein science are increasingly reported with explicit verification, calibration, or provenance rather than as unchecked outputs. ProtoPure applies an LLM-based workflow to extract 12 standardized purification parameters from literature across UniProt proteomes, producing a database. Struct-Caliper supplies query-specific p-values for protein structure search through representation-aware randomization, improving homolog recovery. A pooled E. coli assay quantifies monomeric yield for more than 39,000 proteins, benchmarks inverse folding, and trains the ESMC-MonoYield predictor. The glutamine-removal study ranks residues by replaceability using ProteinMPNN and MSA conservation, with proteome-wide recoding scope of 4,148 E. coli proteins. Not every item involves language models; the shared element is auditable output. What is new is the emphasis on checkable, uncertainty-aware results in both LLM-mediated extraction and predictive modeling of experimental and published data.",
